  "overview": "**UAE Design System** is a light-first design system anchored on `#fcfcfc` canvas surfaces with `#0b0b0c` primary ink (19.2:1 contrast) and `#422ad5` brand accent.\n\nDisplay headlines pair `Inter` with `Roboto` body copy (16px display down to 16px body), unified by `8px` base corner radius and stepped `#fcfcfc` -> `#f9f7ed` surface layering.\n\nMaintained by **UAE**. Source: published token package (https://github.com/TDRA-ae/aegov-dls), repo https://github.com/TDRA-ae/aegov-dls. Inventory: **91** colors, **8** typography steps, and **8** documented components (see repository license).\n\n### Layout & Spacing\n- **Grid & Control Spacing**: Derived from 8 component tokens with documented paddings: `8px 12px`, `2px`, `6px 12px`, `12px 14px`, `10px 14px`.\n- **Hierarchy**: Group controls cleanly within `#f9f7ed` cards; separate sibling sections using `color-mix(in srgb, #0b0b0c 14%, transparent)` hairlines rather than oversized whitespace.\n\n### Elevation & Depth\n- **Surface & Stroke Elevation**: Relies on crisp tonal contrast (`#fcfcfc` -> `#f9f7ed`) and `1px solid color-mix(in srgb, #0b0b0c 14%, transparent)` hairlines instead of heavy drop shadows.\n- **Interactive Lift**: Reserve higher surface brightness or focus outlines anchored on `#422ad5` for keyboard focus and active selection states.",
  "dos": "### Do\n- Anchor base views on `#fcfcfc` (light) with `#0b0b0c` primary text and `#0b0b0c` secondary labels.\n- Use `#422ad5` with `#f7f7f8` text (7.8:1) for primary CTAs, active tabs, and focus outlines.\n- Pair `Inter` headings with `Roboto` body copy using documented weights and scale steps.\n- Apply `8px` base geometry across inputs and buttons (8px on outer containers).\n- Separate containers via `#f9f7ed` surface shifts and `color-mix(in srgb, #0b0b0c 14%, transparent)` hairlines cleanly.\n\n### Don't\n- Do not invert the base canvas out of light polarity without explicitly switching component text tokens.\n- Do not place low-contrast muted ink or raw white text on light accents without verifying >= 4.5:1 WCAG AA contrast.\n- Do not invent arbitrary brand colors, unverified fonts, or synthetic heavy shadows outside the palette above.\n- Do not mix conflicting corner radii that clash with the system's `8px` baseline.\n- Do not truncate or drop border contrast on `input` fields and secondary buttons."
}
